WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.480
Will you eat dinner with me?

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.750
Sensei, will you make and eat dinner with me?

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.780
Why?

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.950
Is that... a no?

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.910
No, it's not that...

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.890
But I'm sure your parents wouldn't want 
you eating with a strange family,

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.750
and it'd be a bother if we used their 
restaurant without permission, right?

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.130
That's not true!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.270
I'll talk to my mother!

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.620
Ooh! What?

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.100
That's not the problem...

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.100
What? What? What?

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.280
I'm inviting you both to come back 
and make a meal with me here.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.020
What? Yay!

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.560
Tsumugi, wait!

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.870
A restaurant!

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.690
I wanna do it!

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.210
Right?!

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.030
Making a cute face doesn't make it okay.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.500
<b>Pork Soup and Restaurant Lights</b>

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.700
I'd really like to add some vegetables.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.420
I should've bought some yesterday 
instead of losing my nerve.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.300
Morning...

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.570
Morning!

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.560
Is it good?

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.950
I can taste the ingredients.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.860
I see.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.070
Tsumugi!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.870
<b>Edamame</b>

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.870
<b>Shrimp Cheese Gratin</b>

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.870
<b>Crab</b>

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.870
Which of these do you like?

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.700
For lunch?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.580
Yup.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:00.710
<b>Shrimp Cheese Gratin</b>

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.240
This one's yummy, and after you eat it,

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.600
there's a picture of an animal on the bottom.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.870
And I like these, too!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:07.600
<b>Crab Cream Croquettes</b>

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:07.600
They're soft and yummy and round and cute!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.070
The others are okay, I guess.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.060
Got it.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.950
Wieners!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.860
Daddy cooked them.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.560
Daddy cooked me wieners...

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:29.830
I told you yesterday that I'd do 
my best to cook a meal, right?

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.010
A meal...

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.620
With Kotori-chan?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.470
No... That's...

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.300
My mother won't mind.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.490
She's busy with other work lately,

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:53.670
so the restaurant is closed a lot.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.360
I like this restaurant and the food!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.530
Daddy said it was good, too!

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.510
I did, but...

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.020
It feels like it'll disappear.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.600
It kind of feels...

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.990
like the restaurant might disappear.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.580
My mom's away a lot.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.390
It doesn't have to be every day.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.500
We could just turn on 
the lights in the restaurant

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.320
and make something to eat 
together once in a while.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:31.430
I want to eat at Kotori-chan's place again!

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.450
Okay, let's use that formula 
to solve a problem.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.400
Okay. Now, who...

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.330
<b>Social Studies Prep Room</b>

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.330
Iida Kotori, huh?

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:57.500
I heard her parents divorced 
when she was in third grade.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.370
Her mother runs a restaurant, and also 
has a role as a cooking expert on TV.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:08.680
It would be a bad idea for me to visit 
the home of a specific student, wouldn't it?

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.230
Well, not many teachers these days interact 
with their students outside school.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.850
But when I was younger,

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.860
we went out to do things with the students,
and had meals at their houses.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.090
Why not meet with Iida-san's 
mother and speak with her?

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.540
Then you can talk about what to do.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.000
If you're coming to me for advice,

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.850
that means you're not sure what to do, right?

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:40.670
Yeah...

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.060
Part of you wants to do it. Am I wrong?

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:49.260
Whether it's for her, or for you.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.370
<b>Remember to gargle!          Wash your hands!</b>

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.600
<b>Remember to gargle!</b>

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.600
You're so good, Tsumugi-chan!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.920
You're so good!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.890
What's that? Poop?

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:01.750
No!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.610
Look, Daddy!

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.610
Um...

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.820
Is that a park?

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.120
It's a Hamburg steak with egg on top 
that Daddy worked really hard to make,

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.540
and I'm eating it, and it's good!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.500
So...

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.910
This is you,

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.850
and this is Daddy?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.450
Who's this?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:30.470
Kotori-chan!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.890
This is Kotori-chan's house!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.800
You really like that place, don't you?

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.470
It's cool,

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:44.020
and you looked good, too!

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:46.150
I looked good, huh?

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.800
The food was good, too!

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.610
I like that place!

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.320
I see. You like it, huh?

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.060
Yup!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.090
You drew a picture of something you like,

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.850
so you should write your name on it.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.060
Okay!

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:23.160
It's only the end of second period.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.290
Sense—

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.880
I'm sorry.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.170
I didn't mean to scare you.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:30.980
No!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.720
Do you come here often?

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.340
Almost every day.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.430
Every day?

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.220
Not many people come here.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.820
Um... Am I not allowed to?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.130
Oh, no.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.300
It's fine.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.500
About what we discussed before...

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.440
About making food to eat at your restaurant.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.120
Yes?

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.550
I'd like to meet with your mother and discuss it.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:03.790
Tell me a day when she's free.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.070
There's no hurry...

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.640
My mom will be home tonight!

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:07.950
No, I didn't...

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:10.440
Feel free to eat at our place, too!

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.700
No, I just want to talk.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.820
Feel free to bring Tsumugi-chan, too!

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:17.530
Um...

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.010
What does Tsumugi-chan like to eat?

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:24.000
Things like Hamburg steak and spaghetti...

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.210
My mom's Hamburg steak is delicious!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.800
Bye, Sensei!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.650
Magi-Magic Magi-Girl Magi-Girl!

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:42.890
Tsumugi,

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.570
The light of hope...

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.750
we're leaving as soon as we get home.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:46.890
Leaving?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.150
<b>Skip Street {This was not right last ep... whoops.}</b>

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.730
I think it was this way...

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.910
We're here!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:01.910
Excuse me.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.830
Kotori-chan, are you the person 
who says, "Welcome"?

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.480
No, I'm apologizing.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.620
Um, where's your mom?

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.740
She got a sudden work call.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.600
It's true.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:18.880
I have a letter from her here.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:21.600
Dear Inuzuka-sensei,
This is Kotori's mother.
I'm very grateful that you'll be 
looking after my daughter.
Please use the kitchen however 
you like. I'm sorry, but I had to 
leave suddenly for work.
 Thank you very much.
Iida Megumi

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.600
I even had her put a thumb print on it.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:22.910
Thumb print?

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:25.260
Should I have had her 
seal it with blood instead?

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.220
Blood?

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.810
That's not the problem.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.670
If she's not here, we'll come another time.

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:33.660
U-Um...

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.150
Will you at least eat dinner before you go?

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.130
Dinner!

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.380
No, we can't...

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.760
I have all the ingredients ready.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.030
What is it?

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:51.310
That's an old one of mine.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.220
Want to wear it?

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.600
Yes!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.780
No, no.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.330
Tsumugi, you can't...

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.430
Daddy!

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.800
Look at me!

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.430
What are we making for dinner?

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.170
Pork soup and Hamburg steak.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.360
Hamburg!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.570
Hamburg! Hamburg! Hamburg!

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.570
Won't you eat before you go?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.320
Daddy, can't we eat before we go?

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.570
Just for today, okay?

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:24.520
Okay!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.030
Just for today!

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.000
Pork soup! Pork soup! Pork soup!

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:38.800
So what do we do?

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.880
Don't worry.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.010
I had my mom write out the recipe.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:51.440
<b>Fry the chopped onions in olive oil,
and when they change color, 
take them out and cool them.
Soak the bread crumbs 
in milk and beat the egg.</b>

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.200
It looks like a picture book...

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.440
I told her there'd be a young child.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.070
A picture book? Let me see!

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.940
Rice, pork soup,

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.940
Onions?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.940
Hamburg steak, salad, mashed potatoes...

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.700
Could we even eat all this?

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:01.700
Frying pan?

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.220
I think the Hamburg steak 
and soup are enough.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.610
I see...

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.910
Oh, the rice is ready to cook.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.090
Let's start with the pork soup.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.460
Cutting the vegetables and making 
the preparations will take time.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:21.670
Okay.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:27.850
So many veggies!

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.520
You're putting all this in?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.210
Do you put potatoes in pork soup?

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.690
Our family does.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.150
Sensei, please cut the vegetables.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.120
Okay.

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.540
Fingers in. Fingers in.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.250
Can I have it?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.300
It's... a present.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.110
Um...

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:22.610
Yes?

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.280
If you don't help,

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.040
I think it's going to take all night...

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:31.690
I-I'll, um... be the taste-tester.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:32.630
Taste-tester?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.860
Sensei, you should try and 
make them all the same size.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.790
I heard they'll all absorb 
different amounts of flavor.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:44.050
Then please cut them with me.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.220
I-I'm, um... That is...

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:55.430
I'm not very good either, but that's 
nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:58.580
I'm sorry.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:02.320
I'm scared of kitchen knives.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.780
I'm scared of knives.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:12.400
There was a knife monster in <i>Magi-Girl,</i> 
and he was scary, wasn't he?

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:20.920
Did you want someone who could 
cut the vegetables for you?

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.910
I know that if I could do it myself...

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:30.550
My mom's busy, so it would 
make her life easier.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.180
But I just can't.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.330
You looked like you were 
having trouble yourself,

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.690
and I knew I could do taste-testing.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.840
So I thought it was a good idea.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.840
It feels like I'm using you.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.700
I'm sorry.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:49.830
Oh, no...

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.090
"Tear the konnyaku apart with 
your hands and parboil it."

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:03.500
That's right.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.840
I'll do it, too!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:08.910
That's right.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.790
You've got an apron on.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.560
Maybe I'll have you help.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.750
Okay!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.690
How about you help, too?

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.610
It's fun to tear it apart!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:27.620
It's sticky and squishy!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:29.820
Okay.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.470
Sticky!

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:32.810
Squishy!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.620
Sticky...

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:37.720
Squishy...

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:40.810
Actually, this makes me feel better.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.250
I really was having trouble.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.120
I wasn't sure

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:50.130
if I could make good food for 
Tsumugi to eat on my own.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.020
So, um...

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:56.550
The restaurant lights that 
you want to leave on...

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.900
When I saw them, I felt really relieved.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:05.610
So I guess, to some degree, 
we can both help each other.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.360
Help each other?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.650
I want Tsumugi's wish to come true.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.780
A bunny!

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.360
I've got a kitty, too!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:18.740
I know!

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.810
I like this one! Can I? Can I?!

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:25.540
Sure.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:33.820
I can't...

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.660
Maybe it's still a little hard.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:38.250
Daddy! Make it thinner!

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.220
L-Leave it to me!

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.650
You boil starting with cold water?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.530
It brings out more flavor, apparently.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.580
<b>Iida Kotori</b>

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.040
What about the meat?

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.170
Let's blanch the meat.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.580
Cooking is...

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.380
hard on the shoulders, huh?

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.050
I know what you mean!

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.780
Daddy cuts!

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:29.930
Kotori-chan tastes!

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.910
And Tsumugi makes the menu!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.530
The menu?

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:36.670
Squid?

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.280
There's no squid in this.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.730
Can you bring me some tape?

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.970
Tsumugi, you can't put that 
up without permission.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:44.410
It's okay.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:46.840
Here.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.040
Thanks!

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.200
Sorry.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.980
I'll take it down when we leave.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.730
We cut the ingredients and put up the menu.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.890
Now it's your turn.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:09.910
You're the taster, right?

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:13.940
Adding flavor is the part I'm worst at.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.760
Take care of it, okay?

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:18.980
Okay.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.880
You're supposed to put in 
set amounts of these, right?

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:25.880
Yes...

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:29.330
But people have individual preferences.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:32.200
So the recipe is just a guideline.

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:36.050
You flavor it little by little, like this.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:48.010
You remember what your mother's 
cooking tastes like, huh?

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.780
I like about this much.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:08.540
It's good.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.720
Looks like we won't get to 
the Hamburg steak, but...

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.530
Shall we eat?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.310
'Kay!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.770
Let's eat!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.370
Yummy!

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.080
Sensei!

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.080
Daddy!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.840
This makes me really happy...

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:01.800
Happy? You're supposed to say it's yummy.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:05.740
Yeah. You saying it's yummy makes me happy.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:06.500
Yeah.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:13.350
The potatoes are hot...

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.560
Make sure you blow on it first.

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:21.820
These potatoes really are good!

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.300
They're so warm and delicious, right?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.760
You can use Japanese yams 
and sweet potatoes, too!

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.830
Rice and pork soup are fantastic together!

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:42.670
Fantastic together!

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:47.010
We'll leave at 8:00.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.640
I need to get Tsumugi to bed.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:53.940
Okay.

00:20:58.470 --> 00:20:59.900
Next is Hamburg steak, right?

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.840
Hamburg steak, and omelet rice,

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.070
and that meatball thing would be good, too!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.330
With Kotori-chan, too!

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.790
Right?

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.140
I...

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.290
That's right.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.720
We can look forward to next time.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.950
Next time?

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:29.820
I want to decide on some rules, 
as well as times,

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:31.220
but we can do that next time.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.930
We'll look forward to it.

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:36.190
Huh? Huh?!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:39.740
It's fun to scramble around 
and make things here.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:44.900
And more than anything, 
it makes Tsumugi happy.

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:51.910
Thank you very much!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.430
Thank you very much!
